# TypeScript

Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes. Always prefix with `I`:

- `IUser`, `IPlan`, `ICreateSaleDto`, `IPaginatedResult`

Use `type` only for unions, intersections, mapped/utility types, primitive aliases.

Never use `any` or `as any`. Use `unknown` + narrow, generics, or Zod parse.

Export shared interfaces from `@zarva/shared`. Feature-local interfaces stay in the feature.

Nest DTOs mirror shared interfaces; Prisma types stay in the repository layer.

React: `interface IXxxProps`; TanStack Query generics required.

Checklist: new public shape has `I*`; no implicit any; typecheck passes.
